Key Frontend Requirements
Area	Frontend Requirement
Authentication	Sign up, login, logout, forgot/reset password, email/OTP verification
User Profile	Name, photo, education, skills/interests, consultation history, assessment history and subscription status
Landing Page	Clear explanation of consulting, courses, assessments, pricing and how the platform works
Expert Discovery	Browse/search consultants by expertise, industry, rating, experience, availability and price
Expert Profile	Bio, skills, experience, consultation fee, ratings/reviews, available slots and Book Consultation button
Consultation Booking	Date/time selection, booking confirmation, upcoming appointments and cancellation/rescheduling
Consultation Interface	Video/meeting link, appointment information, consultant details and session status
Subscription System	Subscription plans, benefits, expiry/renewal date, current plan and upgrade/cancel controls
Payments	Checkout supporting eSewa, Khalti and e-banking, NPR pricing, payment status and transaction history
Courses	Course catalogue, search/filtering, course detail, instructor information, lessons, progress tracking
Course Access Control	Users must pass the required assessment before course content becomes accessible
Locked Course UI	Clearly show why a course is locked and provide a Take Assessment action
Assessment Instructions	Explain exam duration, passing score, camera/screen-sharing rules, warning system and 48-hour lockout
Device Check	Camera permission, screen-share permission, browser compatibility and connection checks before starting
Proctored Assessment UI	Question panel, timer, question navigation, answer selection, camera preview and monitoring status
Cheating Warnings	Visible warning counter: Warning 1/3, 2/3, 3/3
Automatic Disqualification UI	Immediately terminate the assessment after the configured third violation and display the reason/status
48-Hour Lockout	Failed/disqualified candidates see the exact date/time when they may attempt again
Assessment Results	Score, pass/fail status, attempts, feedback and unlocked course access after passing
Student Dashboard	Upcoming consultations, subscriptions, enrolled/unlocked courses, progress and assessment results
Consultant Dashboard	Appointments, availability management, client/session information, earnings and profile management
Admin Frontend	Users, consultants, courses, assessments, questions, subscriptions, payments and reports
Notifications	Booking confirmation, consultation reminders, payment confirmation, assessment results and course access updates
Reviews & Ratings	Users can review consultants after completed consultations
Responsive Design	Full usability on desktop, tablet and mobile
Accessibility	Keyboard navigation, readable typography, proper contrast, accessible forms and error states
Loading/Error States	Skeleton/loading indicators, validation messages, API error handling and retry states
Security UX	Session expiry handling, protected routes, role-based screens and safe payment redirection
Main Frontend Pages

The minimum page structure I would use is:

Public: Home → About/How It Works → Consultants → Consultant Details → Courses → Course Details → Pricing → Login/Register.

User: Dashboard → Profile → My Consultations → Book Consultation → My Courses → Assessment → Assessment Result → Subscription → Payments → Notifications.

Consultant: Dashboard → Profile → Availability → Appointments → Clients → Earnings/History.

Admin: Dashboard → Users → Consultants → Courses → Assessments → Questions → Payments → Subscriptions → Reports.

Important technical requirements
[1:04 PM]Your frontend will also need:

GraphQL client such as Apollo Client
JWT/session authentication
Role-based route guards
WebRTC/browser Media APIs for camera and screen sharing
Assessment timer that is synchronized with the backend
Persistent answers so refreshing does not erase an assessment
Real-time violation/event reporting
Payment callback/status screens
Responsive reusable component system
Form validation
Global notification/toast system